From d74b105de87e49dd2f7e526bd6948a978492d2b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:32:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(app): pocket recognition refuses an inside-out or open
 mesh by name

pockets_of read "up" and "leans into" straight off the facet winding, so
an inside-out cube came back as a closed pocket over its own outline, as
deep as the part - and detect_pockets create would cut it to the base.
It now asks #387's body-winding verdict first and refuses any body whose
outside cannot be trusted (inside-out, open, non-manifold, mixed, flat),
in its own words. Found by the maintainer's review of #512.

Pinned by pocket_recognition::an_inside_out_mesh_is_refused_never_read_as_a_pocket
(fails without the fix: the reversed cube reads as a 10 mm closed pocket)
and the torn-mesh case in degenerate_input_refuses_cleanly.

Fixes #718

